# LOC_DustwalkerArchive -- the one real interior in the starting region.
# Canon: Exodus_Chapter5_Canon.md §2 (LOC_DustwalkerArchive -- Dustwalkers; Information gate)
#        §4 NPC_LastElder (HomeLocation), §6 DOC_DustwalkerOralHistory + DOC_DustwalkerRouteMarks
#        §7 QUEST_150 Reconstruct the Routes
#        docs/Chapter 5_... VII -- "A damaged Dustwalker archive" and
#        "Primary lessons: ... the value of oral knowledge"
#
#   python Scripts/location_brief.py --brief Documentation/World/Briefs/DustwalkerArchive.brief
#
# Deliberately the ONLY enclosed volume among the five POIs. That is a pacing decision:
# the region teaches survival in the open for four sites, then puts the answer indoors,
# below grade, behind a collapse. It is entered through CON_Breach rather than its own
# door -- RULE_BuriedArchiveEntry makes that a hard constraint so the gate is never
# generated shut.

Location:
Dustwalker Archive

Region:
Central Dust Basin

City style:
Vernacular

Purpose:
The Information gate of Act I. A sub-grade record store holding the route language and
the oral history, plus the last living Dustwalker memory. Small footprint, long section:
one room that matters and the shaft that reaches it.

Primary structures:
Buried Archive

Networks:
Route Markers

Traversal:
Interior
Ruin
OpenGround
Track

World state:
Abandoned -> Damaged -> Collapsed

Gameplay:
Locked areas
Vertical traversal
Document recovery
Oral history
Route reading
